[Music]  what could possibly drive the  mild-mannered timothy mcgee from ncis to  take extreme measures that could put his  career on the line keep watching to find  out with countless crime procedural  dramas on the air the jag spin-off ncis  remains one of the most popular and it's  not difficult to see why the cbs series  now in its 19th season follows the  special agents of the naval criminal  investigative services as they work to  solve cases related to the navy and  marine corps the show focuses primarily  on investigating crime and bringing  those responsible to justice but it's  not all business all the time each  episode makes sure to devote some time  to the personal lives of its team  members and explore the unique bonds  they've developed in the field bless you  what are you my priests  curse you considering that the show has  been on the air since september of 2003  it should come as no surprise that the  cast list has seen its share of changes  over the years with veteran actor mark  harmon stepping back from the series as  of october 2021 that leaves only two  original ncis agents in the spotlight  former medical examiner donald mallard  and senior field agent timothy mcgee the  latter specializes in cyber security and  computer crime and tends to stand out  from his colleagues as a dork after all  he writes mystery novels based on their  job on occasion however mcgee will  surprise everyone with a dramatic  attitude shift by asserting himself when  a scenario calls for it like in season 4  episode 9 of ncis where he makes an  uncharacteristically drastic move that  jeopardizes everything he's worked for  and briefly strains most of his personal  and professional relationships the  episode titled twisted sister features  timothy mcgee's hot-headed sibling sarah  arriving at her older brother's  apartment and it doesn't take long to  figure out that something's terribly  wrong she's dazed disheveled and covered  in blood dropping a bombshell right out  of the gate i think i killed someone too  as anyone would be tim's taken aback by  this revelation but he doesn't allow his  emotions to get the best of him instead  he lets her in so she can wash off the  mysterious blood and get some rest in  the morning he calls out of work six so  he can attempt to solve the case without  the rest of the ncis team however when  visiting her college he realizes his  colleagues are investigating a dead  sailor on campus prompting him to flee  the scene though he was certain that  sticking his neck out for his sister was  the right call mcgee soon realizes that  his career threatening choices couldn't  remain a secret forever in this episode  tim seems to make every wrong move for  the sake of protecting sarah after all  she's his sister and despite how guilty  she appears the last thing he wants is  for her life to fall to pieces he does  wisely suggest involving ncis but she  refuses and it isn't until they get  caught trying to sort the situation out  themselves that the truth comes out this  causes everyone to finally work together  to retrace sarah's steps and get some  answers as if he wasn't already in hot  water mcgee's dedication to clearing his  sister's name goes too far when even  after receiving surprising leniency from  ncis despite withholding evidence he  snaps at director jennifer shepard and  quits on the spot of course gibbs once  again proves himself as the glue holding  the ncis team together by convincing him  to stay once his temper is cooled a bit  but it's a genuinely shocking moment all  the same this isn't a side of mcgee that  viewers see too often so when it does  come out you know that something's amiss  thankfully everything works out for the  mcgee family in the end but getting  sarah's complex predicament taken care  of was no easy feat to some extent it's  plain to see why tim's usual  level-headedness totally disappeared in  twisted sister but it's difficult to  deny that he overstepped his bounds on  this particular occasion  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  ncis are coming soon subscribe to our  youtube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]

